        "original_id": "49981379-2b45-5c24-abbc-ebd872865013",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maria Brontë, Patrick Brontë, Elizabeth Brontë, Maria Branwell\n- Organizations: Cowan Bridge School\n- Topics: family relationships, deaths, disease outbreaks\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Brontë was born on 17 March 1777 and later became an Irish priest and author who spent most of his adult life in England.\n- Maria Brontë, née Maria Branwell, was the mother of Maria Brontë.\n- Maria Brontë was born on 23 April 1814 and was the eldest daughter of Patrick Brontë and Maria Brontë, née Maria Branwell.\n- Maria Brontë died on 6 May 1825.\n- At Cowan Bridge School, a typhoid outbreak was followed by the tuberculosis deaths of the sisters Maria and Elizabeth.",
